# Logs — root-anchored so we only ignore the top-level runtime log dirs.
# An UNanchored `logs/` matches any directory named `logs` ANYWHERE in
# the tree, which silently swallows Next.js route segments whose URL
# path includes `/logs` (e.g. `src/app/api/brief-to-ifc/v3/runs/[id]/logs/`).
# Git can't recurse into excluded dirs, so `!path/to/logs/` negations
# don't rescue files inside them — root-anchoring is the only safe fix.
*.log
/logs/
/analytics-logs/

# Generated files (AI tools, reports, scripts)
*.sh
!scripts/check-no-deprecated-image-models.sh
*.txt
